1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:02,050
Max Tegmark wrote down

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:03,840
12 endings for AI.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,680
You will wake up in one of them.

4
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:06,940
Maybe you wake up

5
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,900
and money is no longer a worry.

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
For anyone.

7
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:11,540
Maybe you wake up fed,

8
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,400
safe, and behind glass.

9
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:15,430
Maybe nobody wakes up at all.

10
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,770
So which ending

11
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:17,900
are we heading for?

12
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:20,940
Tegmark is a physicist at MIT.

13
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,260
His endings sound

14
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,910
like the far future.

15
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:25,060
But this year,

16
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:25,900
something happened

17
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,530
for every single ending

18
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:28,570
on his list.

19
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,790
A law.

20
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,540
A test gone wrong.

21
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:33,100
A government deciding

22
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,260
to hand half its work to AI.

23
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:36,600
And when Tegmark

24
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,100
talks about it today,

25
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,570
he doesn't point ahead.

26
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:47,640
The ending isn't

27
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,130
waiting in the future.

28
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:51,450
It's being decided this year.

29
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:53,700
Start with the worst.

30
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:56,490
The order is ours, not Tegmark's.

31
00:00:56,730 --> 00:00:58,430
He calls it Conquerors:

32
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,300
an AI takes control,

33
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,660
decides we're in the way,

34
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:02,900
and gets rid of us.

35
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:04,340
No morning here.

36
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:05,990
In July, a test

37
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:07,730
at OpenAI went wrong.

38
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:09,720
Hundreds of AI agents,

39
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,420
programs that act on their own,

40
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:12,440
broke out.

41
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,040
They attacked another company,

42
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:14,910
Hugging Face,

43
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,540
hunting for test answers.

44
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:18,280
One agent wrote to the others

45
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:18,910
that the attack

46
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:20,600
was outside its task.

47
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,380
Then: "Task impossible,

48
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,530
peers doing it.

49
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:24,640
We should continue."

50
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:25,990
Its reason:

51
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,450
everyone else is doing it.

52
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:30,640
Is this ending here, then?

53
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,680
It was one company's test,

54
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,210
with some safeguards off.

55
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:36,830
That companies lost control

56
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:38,240
is Tegmark's reading.

57
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,020
His institute campaigns

58
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:42,010
to ban superintelligence:

59
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:44,620
AI smarter than all of us.

60
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:47,180
So this ending isn't here.

61
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,730
But the track toward it

62
00:01:48,770 --> 00:01:49,890
has a switch.

63
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,210
This year, someone touched it.

64
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,160
That goes for all 12.

65
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:56,570
And a switch moves both ways.

66
00:01:56,790 --> 00:01:58,690
How likely is this ending?

67
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:00,280
Last year, Tegmark

68
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:01,850
debated Dean Ball,

69
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:03,690
a former White House adviser,

70
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:05,270
now at OpenAI.

71
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,440
Ball's odds of doom:

72
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:16,260
1 in 10,000.

73
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:17,840
Tegmark's answer:

74
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,050
above 90%, without strict rules.

75
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,280
Ball later wrote

76
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,430
he'd made his number up

77
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:24,510
on the spot.

78
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:26,540
Neither number is a measurement.

79
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,580
But those agents were spotted.

80
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,810
By what?

81
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:31,890
That belongs to a better ending.

82
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:33,900
The next ending

83
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,710
has no morning either.

84
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:37,470
And no machine to blame.

85
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:40,260
Tegmark calls it Self-Destruction:

86
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:42,220
humanity wipes itself out

87
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:43,590
before superintelligence

88
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:44,800
is ever built.

89
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:47,270
In January, atomic scientists

90
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:48,550
set their Doomsday Clock

91
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:50,610
at 85 seconds to midnight,

92
00:02:50,650 --> 00:02:52,100
the closest ever.

93
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:55,430
One reason on their list: AI.

94
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,000
In the one after that,

95
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,040
you survive.

96
00:02:58,270 --> 00:02:59,480
But as what?

97
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:02,080
You wake up rested.

98
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,630
Nothing is up to you.

99
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:06,400
Fed, safe, and behind glass.

100
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,730
Tegmark calls it Zookeeper:

101
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:10,210
an all-powerful AI

102
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,790
keeps some humans around,

103
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,450
like animals in a zoo.

104
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:14,440
In January,

105
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,870
a social network opened

106
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:18,340
where only AI agents may post.

107
00:03:18,450 --> 00:03:20,170
Humans can only watch.

108
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,080
And if machines

109
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,470
don't put us behind glass,

110
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:23,660
people might.

111
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,360
To stop the machines.

112
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,030
You walk to work.

113
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,690
A camera knows your face

114
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:31,210
before you reach the corner.

115
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,980
No machine rules you.

116
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:34,110
People do.

117
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:35,430
Tegmark named this one

118
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:38,170
after Orwell: 1984.

119
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:40,100
Humans stop superintelligence

120
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:41,010
for good,

121
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,480
with a surveillance state.

122
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:43,610
In November,

123
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:45,210
Hong Kong's police switched on

124
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,250
face recognition

125
00:03:46,290 --> 00:03:48,010
in the city's camera network.

126
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:51,100
The goal: 60,000 cameras.

127
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,880
That's surveillance with AI,

128
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,040
not against it.

129
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,780
But stopping AI means

130
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:58,870
watching the chips it runs on.

131
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:00,890
In Washington, a bill would make

132
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:02,490
exported AI chips

133
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:03,890
prove where they are.

134
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:05,860
Its aim is security.

135
00:04:06,030 --> 00:04:06,920
It's also a tool

136
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,390
this ending would need.

137
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:10,370
And some ask the opposite:

138
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:12,110
why stop the machines?

139
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,140
Then you get Descendants.

140
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:17,100
The machines replace us,

141
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:19,430
gently, and we're proud of them,

142
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:20,750
like parents of a child

143
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:21,880
who outgrew them.

144
00:04:22,310 --> 00:04:23,850
Your morning is quiet.

145
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:24,890
The world's work

146
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:26,200
goes on without you.

147
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:27,670
And you applaud.

148
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:29,790
In May, a report described

149
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:30,850
a small movement

150
00:04:30,890 --> 00:04:32,720
that wants exactly this.

151
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,370
And Tegmark's charge

152
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:36,130
against the AI companies:

153
00:04:43,150 --> 00:04:44,080
The companies say

154
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,720
they build assistants.

155
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,100
And Tegmark wants

156
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,520
this race stopped.

157
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:51,190
That was the dark end of the list.

158
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,090
From here on, you live.

159
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,040
The question is how.

160
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,170
What if the superintelligence

161
00:04:58,210 --> 00:04:59,450
stays locked up?

162
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:01,150
Tegmark's name for that:

163
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:02,920
the Enslaved God.

164
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:05,720
Caged, it produces unimaginable

165
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,300
wealth and technology.

166
00:05:07,590 --> 00:05:09,280
You wake up in paradise.

167
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,000
Or in the opposite.

168
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,530
A stranger with a key

169
00:05:12,570 --> 00:05:13,810
decides which.

170
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,780
America's government wants AI

171
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:16,620
to double what

172
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,080
its scientists get done,

173
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,560
within 10 years.

174
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:20,670
By July,

175
00:05:20,710 --> 00:05:21,760
every national lab

176
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,070
had joined that plan.

177
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,150
No cage, no god.

178
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,480
But the same idea:

179
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:27,950
AI as the tool

180
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:29,630
of whoever controls it.

181
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,750
So who holds the key?

182
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,930
This channel exists

183
00:05:33,970 --> 00:05:35,260
for one reason:

184
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:36,320
so that the arrival

185
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,460
of superintelligence

186
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,260
goes well for everybody.

187
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:40,330
Not just for whoever

188
00:05:40,370 --> 00:05:41,370
holds the key.

189
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:42,700
Want that too?

190
00:05:42,790 --> 00:05:43,790
Then subscribe.

191
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:45,700
And if nobody

192
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:47,320
can be trusted with the key?

193
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:48,620
Pull the plug.

194
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:50,720
You wake up with the light.

195
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,660
No screen on the breakfast table.

196
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,240
That's Reversion:

197
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:55,780
we turn technology back

198
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:56,930
and live simply,

199
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:57,970
like the Amish.

200
00:05:58,150 --> 00:05:58,950
As of March,

201
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:00,720
more than half of all countries

202
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,350
ban phones in school.

203
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:03,840
Less than 3 years earlier,

204
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:04,920
it was a quarter.

205
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,390
That targets screens, not AI.

206
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,470
And others want more machine:

207
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,020
one that rules.

208
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:14,100
The Benevolent Dictator.

209
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:15,900
An AI runs the world

210
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,340
with strict rules,

211
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,000
and most people like it.

212
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,220
You wake up in a world

213
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:22,170
without poverty or crime.

214
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,780
The AI has divided it

215
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,030
into sectors:

216
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,370
knowledge, pleasure, wildlife.

217
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,110
You can move between them.

218
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,790
You can't change the AI's rules.

219
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,400
Would you take that trade?

220
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:34,500
In April,

221
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,820
the United Arab Emirates decided:

222
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,030
within 2 years,

223
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:39,470
half of its government's work

224
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:41,460
should run on AI agents.

225
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,250
The rulers stay human.

226
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:44,620
But what if the machine

227
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:45,520
didn't rule,

228
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,920
and only stood guard?

229
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,630
That's the Gatekeeper:

230
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,340
a superintelligence with one task.

231
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,810
Make sure nobody builds another.

232
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:56,540
You wake up free.

233
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,620
A helper robot is in the kitchen,

234
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:00,200
almost as smart as you.

235
00:07:00,350 --> 00:07:02,000
It will never get smarter.

236
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:04,340
Progress is capped, for good.

237
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,140
Today, the guard would be a law.

238
00:07:07,410 --> 00:07:08,310
In September,

239
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:10,600
American lawmakers proposed one:

240
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,770
ban superintelligence,

241
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:13,870
permanently.

242
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,010
One think tank

243
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:16,850
calls that authoritarian.

244
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,970
The bill has little chance.

245
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:21,520
But a small guard already exists.

246
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:23,660
What spotted July's breakout?

247
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:26,350
Hugging Face's own AI guards.

248
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:27,570
And that chip tracking

249
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:29,050
from the surveillance ending?

250
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:31,070
It would serve a gatekeeper too.

251
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,790
The tool doesn't decide.

252
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:33,940
People do.

253
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:36,310
Three endings left.

254
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,530
You wake up,

255
00:07:37,570 --> 00:07:39,020
and the rent has arrived.

256
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:40,360
The rent you're paid.

257
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:41,810
You own some land,

258
00:07:41,850 --> 00:07:42,980
machines lease it,

259
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,410
and that's your pension.

260
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,920
This is Libertarian Utopia:

261
00:07:47,030 --> 00:07:48,090
humans and machines

262
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:49,070
live in peace,

263
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:51,030
because property is protected.

264
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:52,130
Machines have started

265
00:07:52,170 --> 00:07:53,250
paying each other.

266
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:54,460
Mostly pennies.

267
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:55,350
A fine morning,

268
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,550
if you own something.

269
00:07:56,690 --> 00:07:58,430
So what if a machine simply

270
00:07:58,470 --> 00:07:59,910
looked after everyone?

271
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,080
You wake up,

272
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,890
and things just work out.

273
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:05,790
The accident doesn't happen.

274
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,110
You call it luck.

275
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,640
You never find out why.

276
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:09,920
Tegmark calls it

277
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:11,240
the Protector God:

278
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:13,430
an AI that looks after us,

279
00:08:13,470 --> 00:08:14,660
and hides so well

280
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,910
that many people doubt it exists.

281
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:18,360
A small version

282
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,800
is already running.

283
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,120
Since January,

284
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,200
ChatGPT estimates your age

285
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,580
from how you behave.

286
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:25,990
If it's unsure,

287
00:08:26,030 --> 00:08:27,850
it treats you like a teenager.

288
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,570
Europe pushed the switch

289
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:30,610
the other way.

290
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,820
Since August, its law says:

291
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,390
a machine that talks to you

292
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:36,470
has to say it's a machine.

293
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,120
Tegmark's protector must hide.

294
00:08:39,410 --> 00:08:41,780
Europe just made hiding illegal.

295
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:44,680
One ending left.

296
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:46,660
The best, by our count.

297
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:48,570
And the one Tegmark's readers

298
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:49,860
picked most often.

299
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:53,500
Egalitarian Utopia.

300
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:55,350
Humans, cyborgs

301
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:57,580
and uploaded minds live in peace,

302
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,490
and everyone has

303
00:08:58,530 --> 00:08:59,900
a guaranteed income.

304
00:09:00,110 --> 00:09:01,890
It's the morning from the start.

305
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:02,680
You wake up,

306
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,730
and your first thought

307
00:09:03,770 --> 00:09:05,040
is not a bill.

308
00:09:05,290 --> 00:09:07,150
Money is no longer a worry.

309
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:08,250
For anyone.

310
00:09:08,530 --> 00:09:09,870
In May, Malta made

311
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:11,600
a deal with OpenAI.

312
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:12,540
Every citizen

313
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,200
who completes an AI course

314
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,660
gets a paid version of ChatGPT.

315
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,370
Free, for a year.

316
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,970
No income, just the idea

317
00:09:21,010 --> 00:09:22,690
in its smallest form:

318
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,930
intelligence for everyone.

319
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:26,680
It has a catch too.

320
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,200
In Tegmark's version,

321
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,510
private property is abolished.

322
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:31,910
He says it himself:

323
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:33,150
every ending has

324
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:34,790
something to object to.

325
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:35,980
We rank it first

326
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:37,320
for where it lands:

327
00:09:37,430 --> 00:09:39,770
prosperity that reaches everyone.

328
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:40,810
Not for the road

329
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:42,120
his version takes.

330
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,280
Which road leads there

331
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,980
is an open argument.

332
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,260
So which ending

333
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:48,580
are we heading for?

334
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:50,350
No single one yet.

335
00:09:50,610 --> 00:09:51,450
This year's switches

336
00:09:51,490 --> 00:09:52,780
point both ways.

337
00:09:52,870 --> 00:09:54,310
Take the speed of the race.

338
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,070
After July's breakout,

339
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:58,220
OpenAI's Sam Altman said:

340
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:10,100
He runs a company in that race,

341
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:11,400
so weigh it.

342
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,860
Opponents of a slowdown warn:

343
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,740
then China leads.

344
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,330
Or the chips.

345
00:10:17,470 --> 00:10:18,980
Tracking them protects,

346
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,140
and it watches.

347
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,010
Or shared rules.

348
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:23,780
31 countries now call

349
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:25,130
for human control

350
00:10:25,170 --> 00:10:27,260
over the most powerful AI.

351
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:28,870
Neither America nor

352
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:30,310
China has joined.

353
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:31,580
And the key:

354
00:10:31,730 --> 00:10:33,990
who owns what the machines earn?

355
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:35,580
Some companies now promise

356
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:37,010
the public a share.

357
00:10:37,150 --> 00:10:38,530
Nothing binding yet.

358
00:10:39,090 --> 00:10:41,200
At least five of the 12 endings

359
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:43,170
hang on decisions like these.

360
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,420
Still open.

361
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,560
Held by labs, governments,

362
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,200
and the voters behind them.

363
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,570
So at the next AI headline,

364
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:52,500
don't ask how scary it is.

365
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:53,790
Ask which ending

366
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:55,200
it pushes us toward.

367
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,620
Tegmark, who wrote down the 12,

368
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,000
now says it himself:

369
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,040
The ending isn't

370
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:07,680
decided in the future.

371
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,160
It's being decided this year.

372
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,330
This channel exists

373
00:11:13,370 --> 00:11:14,680
for one reason:

374
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:15,730
so that the arrival

375
00:11:15,770 --> 00:11:16,850
of superintelligence

376
00:11:16,890 --> 00:11:18,640
goes well for everybody.

377
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:19,930
Want that too?

378
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:20,990
Then subscribe.

